{"id": "EUVD-2026-102260", "enisaUuid": "ab4974db-4297-32b8-b2a6-9c6d44e2b4fb", "description": "libfsapfs through 20260921 contains an integer underflow in libfsapfs_key_encrypted_key_read_data() that allows attackers to trigger heap out-of-bounds reads via crafted KEK attributes. Attackers can supply a crafted encrypted APFS image with malformed HMAC or wrapped KEK attribute lengths to crash fsapfsinfo, pyfsapfs, dfVFS or plaso and read adjacent heap memory before password checks.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:45:11", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libfsapfs-key-encrypted-key-attribute-oob-read", "https://github.com/libyal/libfsapfs/blob/4c7c1c21f3cfc7d35f0b34b8a47f1f1562d27bbb/libfsapfs/libfsapfs_key_encrypted_key.c#L321-L333", "https://github.com/libyal/libfsapfs/blob/4c7c1c21f3cfc7d35f0b34b8a47f1f1562d27bbb/libfsapfs/libfsapfs_key_encrypted_key.c#L528-L540", "https://github.com/libyal/libfsapfs", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libfsapfs-through-20260921-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-libfsapfs-key-encrypted-key-read-data"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111133", "GHSA-6q77-mgpq-cm3g"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "746dfdb9-58b8-361d-8948-91073d688986", "product": {"name": "libfsapfs", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226420260921"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "324fd123-ba00-369a-bd9b-895f16156bc8", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}], "isExploited": false}